     <h1 class="title" title="Nainital Hill Station">Nainital</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p><b>Location:</b> Central Part Of Himalayas,  UttarPradesh<br />
<b>Area:</b> 132sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Beautiful Himalaya.<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 1938m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 18&#176;C - 20&#176;C; Winter 4.3&#176;C - 7.6&#176;C  .<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b>  March-June,September-October     </p>
 <p><b>Main Attractions:</b> Lake, Naina Devi Temple, Mountains </p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/north-india-hill-stations/nainital.jpg" title="Nainital hill station" alt="Nainital hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Nainital" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<p><b>Natural scenic beauty</b> of Nainital is always a shining jewel in the necklace of the Himalayas. Being situated at an altitude of 6360 m above sea level surrounded by mountains and has a cool climate. Nature is besta. The beautiful velvety green meadows are dotted with small lakes of clear water Many. Nainital Lakes won the title of <b>Lake District of India</b>. Nainital gets its name from the famous <b>Naini lake</b> is surrounded by hills studded with attractive villas and cottages. The tourists come here to participate in the core of an exquisite beauty of Nainital, <b>Naini Tal</b>. The beauty is more prounced night. When the lights are turned on and the magic inummerable think everyone in the water becomes spell bound.</p>
<p>The lake is surrounded by seven hills namely, <b>Ayarpata; Deopata; Handi Bandi; Cheena; Alma; Laria Kanta and Sher-ka-Danda</b>. It is a site for adventure sports like yachting, boating and paddling. Long walks through the charming forest in salubrious climate make it favorite of travelers. This charismatic hill station is a prospective health resort too. The hill resorts of <b>Almora, Ranikhet, Bhimtal , Sattal, Haldwani , Kaladhungi , Ramnagar, Bhowali , Ramgarh , Mukteshwar, Naukuchiatal and Kausani</b> too added value to this <b>hill station of Uttaranchal</b>. Nainital is a place to flirt with the scenic beauty of pristine Mother Nature.  </p>

<strong>Sight Seeing in Nainital </strong>
<p>Nainital attracts visitors throughout the year across the country. <b>Goddess Naina Devi</b> flanked Mata Kali and Lord Ganesha presides <b>Naina Devi Temple</b>. Church of St. John in the wilderness lies on the northern part of the city Mallital is a beautiful church with beautiful stained glass exquisite. Hanumangarhi is the temple dedicated to Lord Hanuman pictures as the sunset spectacular. The view of snow-capped Himalayas m. 2270 Snow view is magnificent. You can have city views from the highest peaks, Naina Peak or China Peak in the city. Governor's House or <b>Raj Bhavan Nainital</b> is the Government in the House, which was designed in Victorian Gothic interior. Today, picnic place famous, Tiffin Top, Dorothy or space built in memory of an artist, Dorothy Kellet, by her husband gives an excellent view of the Himalayas.</p>
<p><b>Kilbury</b> is the perfect place to spend the weekend with the wide flora and fauna and is a good place for bird watching too. You can get an overview of the Himalayas, the Terai and Bhabhar here. <b>Guano Hills</b> is perfect for hiking some excellent thick forests. It is also home to rare species of birds. As its name implies Land&#39;s End is the area where he seems to be a piece of land. The views of the mountains that surround it are interesting.</p>
<strong>Shopping</strong>
<p><b>Shopping in Nainital</b> is full of surprises. pedestrian markets, independent stores, open markets contribute to its uniqueness. Mall Road, where you can buy handicrafts, wooden handicrafts, sugar cane sticks, shawls, sweaters, wool hats, juices, jams, candles, decorative pumpkins and colorful.</p>

